<item><title>Mauritania&apos;s national team arrives in Ouagadougou for Africa Cup of Nations qualifier</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-s-national-team-arrives-in-ouagadougou-for-48591b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-s-national-team-arrives-in-ouagadougou-for-48591b/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>The Mourabitounes landed early on Thursday and face Burkina Faso in the third round of qualifying for the 2027 tournament, with a return match in Nouakchott next Tuesday.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:46:54 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mauritanian prosecutors seek charges against 28 in &apos;bloggers from abroad&apos; case</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritanian-prosecutors-seek-charges-against-28-in-bloggers-4028fc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritanian-prosecutors-seek-charges-against-28-in-bloggers-4028fc/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>Charges are sought against 28 people, with arrest warrants requested for seven, over alleged criminal organisation, false information and terrorism financing.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:22:09 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mauritania refers 24 to terrorism investigation team</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-refers-24-to-terrorism-investigation-team-b8a4e1/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-refers-24-to-terrorism-investigation-team-b8a4e1/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>Prosecutors in Nouakchott West have accused 24 individuals of crimes including conspiracy against state security and money laundering.</description><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:42:48 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-refers-24-to-terrorism-investigation-team-b8a4e1/share.jpg" length="38998" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-refers-24-to-terrorism-investigation-team-b8a4e1/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
